      "id": "claim_c636afa5fbfa4f7eba33edaeafc7bf22",
      "statement": "In the approval-queue model, observations (authorizeObservation) are read-only and the gatekeeper must wait for authorization before returning data, while actions (submitAction) are fully asynchronous and only actually carried out when applyAction() is eventually called — so a user can approve queued actions in bulk, possibly hours or days later.",
